CONCLUSION: Z is an explicit, computable divergent point of the
shortcut Collatz map on ZZ_2 -- a counterexample to 2-adic Collatz
constructed along the rewrite route (riding the -17 cycle with
aperiodic defects).  Its integer truncations realize exact
supercritical certificates of every finite length.  By the
rigidity dichotomy, no schema-structured refinement can place
such a point in ZZ; that placement is the Collatz conjecture.

